../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md:11:cyspbot accepts Client-presented OpenID Connect ID Tokens from configured issuers and exchanges only the resulting Verified Subject Tokens for repository-scoped GitHub App installation access tokens. The Client is not authenticated and is not assumed to be the ID Token Subject. The important security properties are:
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md-12-
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md:13:- issuer trust is configured, not discovered from Client-presented tokens
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md:14:- the Verified Subject Token is derived only from signed claims in an ID Token accepted through an exact OIDC Provider Registration and its OIDC ID Token Profile
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md:15:- the ID Token audience must be the exact single string `cyspbot`; the unsupported token-exchange `audience` parameter grants nothing
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md:16:- each configured Fly.io organization has its own OIDC ID Token Profile and OIDC Provider Registration; Fly Machine authentication binds the configured organization to the signed organization, Fly App, and Machine names in the canonical Subject, while Token Policy separately selects any provider-assigned IDs needed for authorization
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md:17:- Google service account identity requires a service account ID Token from the Google Cloud IAM authorization server with Issuer Identifier `https://accounts.google.com`; its Authorized Party must equal its non-empty Subject; policy compares the service account unique ID as an opaque string and may additionally require a verified email
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md:18:- Clients must supply exactly one effective canonical repository resource; value-less occurrences are omitted, and subject-token claims never select the target
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md-19-- Clients may request an exact GitHub App permission scope
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md:20:- Token Policy must explicitly allow the Verified Subject Token, GitHub App, resource, and permission combination before a token is issued
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md-21-- the GitHub App installation remains the upper-bound authority for repositories and permissions
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md-22-- the GitHub App private key remains inside the deployment secret boundary
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md-23-- webhook processing requires GitHub signature validation before state changes
../cyspbot-deploy/src/cyspbot/SECURITY.md-24-- webhook deliveries must identify the configured GitHub App before they are accepted
