# Source pin

The deployable source is the public `chikachow/github-app-token-broker`
submodule at `src/github-app-token-broker`.

The accepted source baseline is:

- pull request: <https://github.com/chikachow/github-app-token-broker/pull/8>
- branch: `main`
- merged commit: `55331b13ffd1261816ee27df121c7c9ca1cad1bc`

Production preflight requires the merged PR #8 baseline and the pinned commit
itself to be ancestors of current source `main`. The check depends only on
objects reachable from `main`, so it also works in the shallow submodule checkout
used by the deployment workflow. That is the accepted-source gate; a branch name
or open pull request is not sufficient.

`update-github-app-token-broker.yml` advances the pin to the exact remote `main`
commit and opens a signed update pull request.

This pull request's reviewed gitlink update is the initial transition to the
Subject-Token Audience and derived Token Exchange Endpoint action contract. The pre-transition
`2f9a22e8` client asks GitHub for an ID token whose audience is its endpoint URL,
so it cannot authenticate to a Worker enforcing the exact Subject-Token Audience
and must not be used to bootstrap this pin. The automated update workflow
becomes usable only after the revised source is accepted and the coordinated
deployment establishes the new contract.

The pinned source owns the reusable Worker implementation, strict use of the
deployment binding `TOKEN_BROKER_AUDIENCE` as the exact Subject-Token Audience,
portable policy and OIDC Provider Registration Interfaces, source-side action
integrations, and dispatch workflow. This repository owns its reviewed OIDC
Provider Registrations, Token Issuance Policy, and Worker entrypoint. The root
workspace consumes the pinned packages directly; the public repository is also
installed and checked independently with its own lockfile. The Subject-Token Audience is
exactly `https://cyspbot.chikachow.org`. `TOKEN_BROKER_URL` is not a Worker
binding. The separately released `cyspbot-app-token-action`, pinned here at
bundled release commit `bf8d299cd20f755c47feb733e3c0f56331a4b49e`
(`v0.0.12`), uses the same fixed Subject-Token Audience and defaults to
`https://cyspbot.chikachow.org/token` without consulting a request
URL, `Host`, or forwarded headers.

Neither the OIDC Provider Registrations nor Token Issuance Policy is a runtime
override. Changing either requires a reviewed deployment-source change, a new
bundle, and deployment of that artifact.

The pinned source workflows use the independently bundled action release
without a `cyspbot-token-url` override. Its `pnpm-up` workflow relies on the
action's default endpoint, repository resource, and least-privilege scope. Its
deployment-update workflow relies on the default endpoint while explicitly
requesting the deployment repository and `actions:write`. This repository's
own source-update workflow currently supplies its configured endpoint plus an
explicit deployment-repository resource and scope. The deployment validates
the Worker's Subject-Token Audience against the action's Subject-Token Audience
and independently validates the action's effective Token Exchange Endpoint
against the full routed `/token` URL before deployment or an automated source
update. A future endpoint-only migration can set the URL override without
rotating the Subject-Token Audience.
